1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,017
A distance, time graph shows how an object moves.

2
00:00:03,017 --> 00:00:07,361
Time goes along the horizontal axis, and distance up the vertical axis.

3
00:00:07,361 --> 00:00:12,368
A flat, horizontal line means the object isn't moving: its distance stays the same.

4
00:00:13,429 --> 00:00:19,341
A straight line sloping upwards means a constant speed: the same distance is covered every second.

5
00:00:20,402 --> 00:00:25,832
A curved line means the speed is changing. If it gets steeper, the object is speeding up.

6
00:00:25,832 --> 00:00:29,090
The steeper the line, the faster the object is moving.

7
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:31,477
Let's plot Lee's run.

8
00:00:31,477 --> 00:00:37,752
First, he runs 8 kilometres in 1 hour at a constant speed: a straight line sloping upwards, from A to B.

9
00:00:38,812 --> 00:00:44,785
Then he rests for half an hour. His distance doesn't change, so the line from B to C is horizontal.

10
00:00:45,846 --> 00:00:51,879
Finally, he runs another 8 kilometres, taking 1.5 hours. The line from C to D slopes upwards again,

11
00:00:51,879 --> 00:00:55,861
but it's less steep than A to B, because he's running more slowly.

12
00:00:56,921 --> 00:01:01,688
Graphs help us compare. A cheetah and a man start running from the same place.

13
00:01:01,688 --> 00:01:05,368
The cheetah's line is very steep at first: it's much faster.

14
00:01:05,368 --> 00:01:10,798
But after about 20 seconds, its line goes flat. The cheetah has stopped, after 400 metres.

15
00:01:11,859 --> 00:01:15,479
The man's line is less steep, but it keeps rising steadily.

16
00:01:15,479 --> 00:01:18,797
He can't match the cheetah's speed, but he keeps going.

17
00:01:19,857 --> 00:01:25,348
Where the two lines cross, the man overtakes the cheetah, and he carries on to 800 metres.

18
00:01:25,348 --> 00:01:28,063
Fast isn't everything: endurance matters too!

19
00:01:29,123 --> 00:01:33,889
A cyclist rides to school. Her distance from home is recorded every 20 seconds.

20
00:01:34,950 --> 00:01:40,742
For the first 40 seconds the line is straight and steep: she covers 100 metres every 20 seconds.

21
00:01:41,802 --> 00:01:46,267
From 40 to 60 seconds the line is flat while she waits at traffic lights.

22
00:01:46,267 --> 00:01:49,042
Then she rides on, but the line is less steep.

23
00:01:50,102 --> 00:01:53,843
Pause and decide: what was her speed in the first 40 seconds,

24
00:01:53,843 --> 00:01:57,101
and was she faster or slower after the traffic lights?
